## Common Patterns

### Creating a New Component
1. Create component file: `src/components/ComponentName.tsx`
2. Define props interface
3. Use shadcn/ui components when possible
4. Export from component file
5. Add to barrel export if shared

### Adding a New Message Type
1. Add type to `MessageType` in `src/shared/messages.ts`
2. Create payload interface
3. Add handler in service worker `handleMessage()`
4. Update type definitions

### Adding Storage Type
1. Update `StorageType` in `src/shared/types.ts`
2. Add handling in `StorageManager`
3. Update UI (popup/options)
4. Add tests

## Dependencies

### Adding Dependencies
- Check if shadcn/ui component exists first
- Prefer lightweight libraries
- Consider bundle size impact
- Document why dependency is needed

### Updating Dependencies
- Test thoroughly after updates
- Check for breaking changes
- Update types if needed
- Update documentation

## Build & Development

### Build Commands
- `npm run build` - Production build
- `npm run type-check` - Type checking only
- `npm run dev` - Development server

### Development Workflow
1. Make changes in `src/`
2. Run `npm run type-check` to verify types
3. Run `npm run build` to build
4. Reload extension in Chrome
5. Test functionality

## Chrome Extension Specific

### Manifest V3 Compliance
- Service workers are stateless
- Use `chrome.scripting` instead of `chrome.tabs.executeScript`
- Event listeners at top level
- Use promises for async operations

### Debugging
- Service worker: `chrome://serviceworker-internals/`
- Content script: Regular DevTools
- Popup: Right-click extension icon → Inspect
- Options: Right-click options page → Inspect

## React Migration Notes

### Current State
- React dependencies installed
- shadcn/ui configured
- Popup/Options still vanilla TypeScript
- Migration in progress

### Migration Guidelines
- Convert one page at a time (popup first, then options)
- Keep existing message passing logic
- Use shadcn/ui components for UI
- Maintain all existing functionality
- Test thoroughly after migration

